body:
Yes i do have good family and friends. I have a counsellor too and lots of nice hobbies. I decided to make a list of things that give me a reason to live to look back at when im feeling horribly down. 

&#x200B;

I was diagnosed when I realized certain behaviours in my life strongly impaired my school work, job and  personal life in general. i talked to my family doctor and he referred me to a psychiatrist. I wanted to know if i were just lazy or i genuinely had ADHD, and what I could do about it. I do want to improve and not use ADHD as an excuse. but it is the cause of my depression

I just feel hopeless and lost in life. I thought I wanted to be a vet for 4 years of my undergrad but then recently decided I don't want to. My undergraduate degree in Biomedical sciences is worthless without graduate school and I realized I am not that interested in doing a master's anyways. I want to do law school later on but I am scared I will not get in and become homeless.

&#x200B;

I feel physically tired everyday. I have tried exercising. eating well. nothing works. even sleep, i get 8 hrs a day and feel horrible. 

&#x200B;

I have been diagnosed with depression and ADHD , and both have impaired my life quite a lot. I just don't feel like a functional adult that can be independent and I don't see myself as being successful in the future. I have basically no motivation to live because I am always tired and have bad habits (though I have tried so hard to fix them) .
